{"id": 3973090, "title": "CVE-2026-82208: wolfSSL CA-cache hit overrides callback", "submitted": "2026-08-27", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3973090", "excerpt": "## Summary\n\nWith the wolfSSL backend, when CA caching is enabled and an `CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION` callback replaces the trust store, curl can silently reinstall the cached store after the callback returns. A certificate trusted by the cached store but rejected by the callback-selected store is then incorrectly accepted.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store()` in `lib/vtls/wolfssl.c` installs a cached X509 store but does not set `wssl->x509_store_setup = TRUE`. That flag is only set inside `wssl_populate_x509_store()`, which runs on cache misses.\n\nThe sequence on a cache hit:\n\n1. Before invoking the callback, `wssl_connect_step1()` calls `Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store()` — cached store A is installed, flag stays `false`.\n2. The `CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION` callback runs and replaces store A with store B.\n3. During the handshake, the still-false flag causes `Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store()` to run again. It finds `CTX_get_cert_store() != cached_store` (the callback changed it), so it reinstalls cached store A.\n\n## Affected versions\n\nIntroduced in commit `0f2876b2c33f` (Jul 2024, \"wolfSSL: CA store share fix\" for #14278). Present in releases **8.9.1 through 8.21.0**.\n\n## Impact\n\nAn application that uses `CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION` to restrict trust (e.g. pin to a private CA) has that restriction silently bypassed when CA caching is active. A MITM presenting a certificate valid under the cached store but rejected by the callback's store succeeds.\n\nPrerequisites: wolfSSL backend, `CURLOPT_CA_CACHE_TIMEOUT != 0`, a callback that replaces the store, and differing trust between the two stores.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Build an affected curl release (8.9.1 through 8.21.0) against wolfSSL and configure curl without a compiled-in default CA path so that a CA file is eligible for caching.\n2. Create two independent certificate authorities, called CA A and CA B.\n3. Create a TLS server certificate for the test hostname, including a matching subject alternative name, and sign it with CA A.\n4. Start an HTTPS server on the test hostname using that certificate.\n5. Write a small libcurl client that uses the same multi handle for two transfers, sets `CURLOPT_CAINFO` to CA A, and sets a nonzero `CURLOPT_CA_CACHE_TIMEOUT`.\n6. Make the first transfer without an SSL-context callback. Confirm that it succeeds and thereby populates curl's CA cache with the trust store containing CA A.\n7. Fo", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "likely_valid", "final_label": "Confirmed by the code", "tone": "good", "explain": "The real code shows the flaw the report describes.", "confidence": 0.95, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "partially_grounded", "rev": "b73a4f00b2a6", "rev_source": "master on 2026-08-27", "counts": {"grounded": 10, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 1}, "problems": [{"check": "symbol", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "CTX_get_cert_store", "evidence": "CTX_get_cert_store() does not exist in curl at b73a4f00b2a6 or in any release since 7.50"}]}, "summary": "curl can silently reinstall a cached CA store after an SSL_CTX_FUNCTION callback replaces it, causing a callback-selected trust store to be bypassed when CA caching is enabled.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store() installs a cached X509 store but does not set wssl->x509_store_setup = TRUE", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The claim accurately describes the vulnerable releases (8.9.1–8.21.0). The release code shows the flag is not set on cache hits; master already contains the fix.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 778, "note": "In release 8.21.0, Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store() lacks the flag set at function entry; wssl->x509_store_setup is only set inside wssl_populate_x509_store() at line 584", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c", "line": 801, "note": "In current master (b73a4f00b2a6), the flag is set at line 801: 'wssl->x509_store_setup = TRUE;' — this is the fix from commit ed0338befd", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "in lib/vtls/wolfssl.c", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "File location confirmed in both master and release versions.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c", "line": 790, "note": "Function definition at line 790 in master; at line 778 in release 8.21.0", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "CA caching is enabled and an CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION callback replaces the trust store", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "CA caching is controlled by CURLOPT_CA_CACHE_TIMEOUT (ca_cache_timeout). The callback CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION is a documented curl option that can replace the wolfSSL context's cert store.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 791, "note": "cache_criteria_met checks data->set.general_ssl.ca_cache_timeout != 0 at line 791", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c", "line": 806, "note": "Same check at line 806 in master", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "a certificate trusted by the cached store but rejected by the callback-selected store is then incorrectly accepted", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "In vulnerable releases, the missing flag allows a second Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store() invocation during handshake to overwrite the callback's store with the cached store, causing incorrect acceptance.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 800, "note": "On cache hit, cached store is installed (line 805) but flag not set; subsequent call reinstalls it (line 805 again) after callback replaces it", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c", "line": 815, "note": "Master fixes this by setting flag at line 801 before cache check", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "use a multi handle, set CURLOPT_CAINFO to CA A, set a nonzero CURLOPT_CA_CACHE_TIMEOUT, make a first transfer to populate the cache, then a second transfer with a callback that replaces the store with only CA B", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "Reproduction steps are concrete and map to the code path: first transfer populates cache (cache miss → wssl_populate_x509_store sets flag), second transfer with callback hits cache but flag remains false in vulnerable code, allowing overwrite.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 791, "note": "ca_cache_timeout check enables caching", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c", "line": 806, "note": "Same in master", "valid": true}]}], "external_checks": [], "external_sources": [{"url": "http://www.wolfssl.com/docs", "title": "Documentation - wolfSSL", "for": "the flag is only set inside wssl_populate_x509_store()"}, {"url": "http://wolfssl.com/docs", "title": "Documentation - wolfSSL", "for": "the flag is only set inside wssl_populate_x509_store()"}, {"url": "https://www.wolfssl.com?p=22", "title": "Documentation - wolfSSL", "for": "the flag is only set inside wssl_populate_x509_store()"}], "key_reasons": ["The release version (curl-8_21_0) shows Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store() does not set wssl->x509_store_setup on cache hits, while master (b73a4f00b2a6) does at line 801 via commit ed0338befd.", "The flaw allows a cached CA store to silently override a CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION callback's store, bypassing the application's trust policy — a clear security impact.", "Reproduction steps are specific, actionable, and match the code path in the vulnerable releases.", "The fix is in master but not in any released version (8.9.1–8.21.0), so the vulnerability exists in production releases."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report. The issue is confirmed in releases 8.9.1 through 8.21.0: Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store() in lib/vtls/wolfssl.c does not set wssl->x509_store_setup on cache hits, allowing a cached store to overwrite a CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION callback's store. The fix (commit ed0338befd) is in master but not yet released. We will include it in the next release. Your reproduction steps are clear and will be used for verification.", "code": [{"name": "lib/vtls/wolfssl.c", "start": 790, "end": 844, "reason": "definition of Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store", "rows": [{"n": 790, "text": "CURLcode Curl_wssl_setup_x509_store(struct Curl_cfilter *cf,", "notes": ["C2: Function definition at line 790 in master; at line 778 in release 8.21.0"]}, {"n": 791, "text": "                                    struct Curl_easy *data,", "notes": []}, {"n": 792, "text": "                                    struct wssl_ctx *wssl)", "notes": []}, {"n": 793, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 794, "text": "  struct ssl_primary_config *conn_config = Curl_ssl_cf_get_primary_config(cf);", "notes": []}, {"n": 795, "text": "  struct ssl_config_data *ssl_config = Curl_ssl_cf_get_config(cf, data);", "notes": []}, {"n": 796, "text": "  CURLcode result = CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 797, "text": "  WOLFSSL_X509_STORE *cached_store;", "notes": []}, {"n": 798, "text": "  bool cache_criteria_met;", "notes": []}, {"n": 799, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 800, "text": "  /* We do not want to do this again, no matter the outcome */", "notes": []}, {"n": 801, "text": "  wssl->x509_store_setup = TRUE;", "notes": ["C1: In current master (b73a4f00b2a6), the flag is set at line 801: 'wssl->x509_store_setup = TRUE;' — this is the fix from commit ed0338befd"]}, {"n": 802, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 803, "text": "  /* Consider the X509 store cacheable if it comes exclusively from a CAfile,", "notes": []}, {"n": 804, "text": "     or no source is provided and we are falling back to wolfSSL's built-in", "notes": []}, {"n": 805, "text": "     default. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 806, "text": "  cache_criteria_met = (data->set.general_ssl.ca_cache_timeout != 0) &&", "notes": ["C3: Same check at line 806 in master", "C5: Same in master"]}, {"n": 807, "text": "    conn_config->verifypeer &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 808, "text": "    !conn_config->CApath &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 809, "text": "    !conn_config->ca_info_blob &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 810, "text": "    !ssl_config->primary.CRLfile &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 811, "text": "    !conn_config->native_ca_store;", "notes": []}, {"n": 812, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 813, "text": "  cached_store = cache_criteria_met ? wssl_get_cached_x509_store(cf, data)", "notes": []}, {"n": 814, "text": "                                    : NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 815, "text": "  if(cached_store &&", "notes": ["C4: Master fixes this by setting flag at line 801 before cache check"]}, {"n": 816, "text": "     wolfSSL_CTX_get_cert_store(wssl->ssl_ctx) == cached_store) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 817, "text": "    /* The cached store is already in use, do nothing. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 818, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 819, "text": "  else if(cached_store && wolfSSL_X509_STORE_up_ref(cached_store)) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 820, "text": "    wolfSSL_CTX_set_cert_store(wssl->ssl_ctx, cached_store);", "notes": []}, {"n": 821, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 822, "text": "  else if(cache_criteria_met) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 823, "text": "    /* wolfSSL's initial store in CTX is not shareable by default.", "notes": []}, {"n": 824, "text": "     * Make a new one, suitable for adding to the cache. See #14278 */", "notes": []}, {"n": 825, "text": "    WOLFSSL_X509_STORE *store = wolfSSL_X509_STORE_new();", "notes": []}, {"n": 826, "text": "    if(!store) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 827, "text": "      failf(data, \"SSL: could not create a X509 store\");", "notes": []}, {"n": 828, "text": "      return CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;", "notes"